From 772544ffaaaa5c16b52e91c75390a2ce6cf11708 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:22:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] Fix the clustering, ds_param and FSM issues met by the
 Pyrenees tutorial

- clustering: the mask, the groups and the cluster maps assumed the
  dimension order of a dataset built from the DEM (x, y); with ds_param.nc
  read from disk (y, x) the mask was misapplied and the maps scrambled.
  Rows are now taken in (y, x) order explicitly. Variables of a previous
  clustering are dropped before re-clustering (pandas 3 failed on the old
  string labels), and the point names outside the mask are set with .loc
  (chained assignment left every pixel at -9999 with pandas 3)
- compute_dem_param: a complete ds_param.nc is loaded, not rewritten
  (minutes for large DEMs, and a second 10-bit quantization)
- FSM: the namelist gets the forcing time step (dt, inferred from the
  forcing file by default; FSM assumed 3600 s, wrong for 3h/6h ERA5);
  read_pt_fsm parses the headerless FSM output with pandas >= 2;
  fsm_sim_parallel accepts a list of files (NameError), sorts them and
  runs the executables in threads (no re-import of the main script, no
  fork of a process holding locks)
- tests/test_workflow.py (the FSM run needs FSM_EXEC)

The FSM changes follow the workshop patch of TPS-tutorials.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012FMkEYDUJxvxmd3SbUsJfP
